id: spectator
name: Spectator
kind: state
# A Special State (the user's terminology): no Narrative Requirement - only an effect that gives it enters it.
specialState: true
description: >
  Out of the fight for now: you watch, you recover, and you call encouragement to an ally.
text: >
  (1)-[Triggered/Spectator, Triggered/Start of Turn]: Target an Ally. Increase their Combat Rolls by 1(bT) until the start of your next turn or until you leave the Spectator State (whichever occurs first).
  (2)-[Triggered/Start of Turn]: Exit the Spectator State.
  (3)-[Automatic/Start of Turn]: If you did not use the second effect of the Spectator State, you lose all of your Actions (except Counter Actions), end your turn, and regain 2d10(bT) Life and Ki Points.
  (4)-[Passive]: You cannot use the Power Up Maneuver, the Transformation Maneuver, the Energy Charge Maneuver, or any Attacking Maneuvers, Special Maneuvers, or Unique Abilities that target another Character.
  (5)-[Passive]: You cannot trigger any [Triggered/Start of Turn] or [Triggered/Start of Combat Round] effects, except those from the Spectator State.

---

# (1) On entering it, and as your turn begins while still in it: which Ally asked - Cheered on them, its stacks your base Tier,
# till the start of your next turn on your clock, and off as you leave the State (chat.mjs spectatorCheer, spectatorLeft).
[triggered/state/spectator]
spectatorCheer();

[triggered/start-of-turn]
spectatorCheer();

[on removed]
spectatorLeft();

# (2) Asked as the turn begins, before its Moment (combat.mjs beginTurn, chat.mjs spectatorTurnStart): left, (3) and (1)'s
# start-of-turn are no longer yours. It used to be a button on the turn's card - which came after (3) had already ended the
# turn.

# (3) Still a Spectator once (2) was asked: no Actions, the turn ended - a skip, which is the same thing at its start - and
# 2d10(bT) Life and Ki Points.
[automatic/start-of-turn]
actions.remaining = 0;
turn.skip = true;
life.value += 2d10(bT);
ki.value += 2d10(bT);

# (4) The three named Maneuvers by name; the rest by their class. "That target another Character" is left applied to none
# of them - which it qualifies is one sentence and three readings.
[passive]
forbid maneuver.power-up;
forbid maneuver.transformation;
forbid maneuver.energy-charge;
forbid attackingManeuvers;
forbid specialManeuvers;
forbid uniqueAbilities;

# (5) Read where a turn's or a Round's start is answered - its Moment and its card: no Triggered effect but this State's
# (moments-runtime.mjs spectatorHeld, chat.mjs momentTriggers).
